mHC reproduction (mhc-repro)
Copyright (c) 2026 Poisson Labs

This product uses software, datasets and tokenizer data from third parties, listed
below. mhc-repro itself is distributed under the MIT licence; see LICENSE.

No third-party source file is vendored in this repository, and no source file in it
carries a third-party copyright notice or licence header. Everything below is
installed or downloaded when the code runs. No pretrained model weights are used:
every model is trained from random initialisation.

Each entry names the page or file the terms were read from. Where an upstream
project states no licence, the entry says so and quotes none.

================================================================================
Papers implemented
================================================================================
The code implements the method of the two papers below from their descriptions and
equations. Neither paper is a source of code or data in this repository.

1. Z. Xie, Y. Wei, H. Cao, C. Zhao, C. Deng, J. Li, D. Dai, H. Gao, J. Chang, K. Yu,
   L. Zhao, S. Zhou, Z. Xu, Z. Zhang, W. Zeng, S. Hu, Y. Wang, J. Yuan, L. Wang,
   W. Liang. "mHC: Manifold-Constrained Hyper-Connections", arXiv:2512.24880, 2025.
   https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.24880

2. D. Zhu, H. Huang, Z. Huang, Y. Zeng, Y. Mao, B. Wu, Q. Min, X. Zhou.
   "Hyper-Connections", arXiv:2409.19606, 2024. https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.19606

3. R. Sinkhorn and P. Knopp. "Concerning nonnegative matrices and doubly stochastic
   matrices", Pacific Journal of Mathematics 21(2), 343-348, 1967.
   https://doi.org/10.2140/pjm.1967.21.343

================================================================================
Datasets
================================================================================

1. C4 (Colossal Clean Crawled Corpus), English configuration `allenai/c4`  [Part 2]
   Upstream: https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/c4
   Source read: https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/c4/raw/main/README.md
   Citation:
     - C. Raffel, N. Shazeer, A. Roberts, K. Lee, S. Narang, M. Matena, Y. Zhou,
       W. Li, P. J. Liu. "Exploring the Limits of Transfer Learning with a Unified
       Text-to-Text Transformer", arXiv:1910.10683, 2019.
   Licence terms status:
     The dataset card's metadata reads `license: odc-by` and its "Licensing
     Information" section reads:

       We are releasing this dataset under the terms of
       [ODC-BY](https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/by/1-0/). By using this,
       you are also bound by the [Common Crawl terms of
       use](https://commoncrawl.org/terms-of-use/) in respect of the content
       contained in the dataset.

     Terms of the linked pages (ODC-BY 1.0 and the Common Crawl terms of use) are not
     restated here. The dataset is streamed at run time by the `datasets` library and
     no part of it is stored in this repository.

2. TinyShakespeare  [Part 1]
   Upstream: https://github.com/karpathy/char-rnn (data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt,
   1,115,394 bytes, downloaded by src/train.py from
   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt)
   Source read: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/karpathy/char-rnn/master/Readme.md
   Licence terms status:
     The repository has no LICENSE file and GitHub reports no licence for it, so no
     licence grant is quoted. Its Readme describes the file as "a subset of works of
     Shakespeare". The text is downloaded when the code first runs and is not
     redistributed here (`data/` is git-ignored).

================================================================================
Tokenizer
================================================================================
GPT-2 byte-pair encoding, loaded by Part 2 through `tiktoken.get_encoding("gpt2")`
  tiktoken (checked in version 0.8.0) downloads, at run time:
    https://openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net/gpt-2/encodings/main/vocab.bpe
    https://openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net/gpt-2/encodings/main/encoder.json
  These are the vocabulary files of OpenAI's GPT-2 release. No separate terms for the
  two files were read; the licence of the release's repository is quoted instead:
